---
// Medicare made simple: Supplement vs Advantage, no prices, no superlatives.
import { site } from '../../data/site';

---

<section class="section" id="medicare" aria-labelledby="medicare-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="medicare-heading">
        Confused by Medicare? That’s normal — and it’s exactly what I’m here for.
      </h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Most people come to me with one big question: Supplement or Advantage?
        Here’s the short version.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cards cards--2">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Medicare Supplement (Medigap)</h3>
        <p>
          Works alongside Original Medicare to help pay what it leaves behind —
          deductibles, copays, coinsurance. See any doctor who accepts Medicare.
          Fewer surprise costs, usually a higher monthly premium.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Medicare Advantage (Part C)</h3>
        <p>
          An all-in-one alternative from private carriers. Many plans include
          extras like prescription, dental, or vision. Usually a lower premium —
          you work within the plan’s network.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="medicare-cta">
      <p>
        There’s no one-size-fits-all answer — it depends on your doctors, your
        prescriptions, and your budget. That’s the conversation I have with every
        client, free of charge.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn--gold" href={site.phoneHref}>Talk to Lisa · {site.phone}</a>
      <p class="microline">Calling connects you with Lisa, a licensed insurance agent.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- VIDEO ASSET PENDING: swap this frame for the real 2-minute explainer -->
    <div class="video-placeholder" role="img" aria-label="Video coming soon">
      <span class="play-ring" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/></svg>
      </span>
      <p>2-minute explainer — coming soon</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
